MerkleAdapterFlowHistory
├── when capital moves between the vault and portfolio
│   ├── it makes allocations immediately available after a long report delay
│   ├── it checkpoints only completed net transfers at end of block
│   ├── it preserves older checkpoints and overwrites same-block values
│   └── it returns the latest recorded flow for current and future block queries
├── when a report arrives after its snapshot
│   ├── it adds subsequent allocations exactly once
│   ├── it subtracts subsequent withdrawals exactly once
│   ├── it avoids subtracting withdrawals already included in the snapshot
│   └── it separates investment performance from both directions of capital flow
├── when cash moves within the portfolio
│   ├── it leaves capital flow unchanged for push, pull and direct account returns
│   └── smaller requests preserve outstanding demand without changing NAV or flow
└── when returned profits exceed lifetime allocations
    ├── it preserves a signed negative cumulative flow
    └── it still reconciles later reports and new allocations
